WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.233
We've

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:02.402
done in our politics is create

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:06.039
a situation where we're electing idiots

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.241
and

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.581
and so

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.982
I don't look at it

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.384
through the lens of like, you know,

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.019
is this what I should do or what

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:19.586
I shouldn't do?

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:20.820
I look at it through the lens of

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.922
how do we elect serious people?

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.058
And I think electing serious people

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.460
can't be partizan.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.596
We're back now with GOP

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.698
presidential candidate Asa Hutchinson.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.266
Some laughs there in the room for that,

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.634
but she's making a serious point.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.404
Do you think it's a fair one?

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.140
Well, of course I disagree

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.908
about the characterization.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:42.609
I've been elected

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.310
governor twice in Arkansas,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.112
and I look at my colleagues

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.580
across the country.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.150
They really have a public mindedness.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.052
They're very bright and credible.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:52.952
Something tells me she

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.521
wasn't talking about same way

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.390
Well, I know that,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.358
but I'm making the point.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.360
There's really good people that serve.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.128
And even if you look at the ones

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:02.929
running for president,

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.065
there's 12 Republicans running.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.132
Most of them are serious.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.468
Candidates that bring great credentials.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.437
I think our point, obviously,

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.572
is that we need candidates

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.907
and we need elected leaders

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.241
that have courage.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.743
They stand for convictions

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.877
that speak the truth

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.079
and do not always listen

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.181
to the loudest voice in the room.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.248
That's what I believe

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.284
the American people want and need.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.754
And also it reminds me that our founding

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.855
fathers understood

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.091
that we're all humans and we're flawed.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.392
And so that's why

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.427
there's a system of checks and balances.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.795
And that's why

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.563
we have the different

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.530
branches of government.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.632
The United States Supreme Court today

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.469
really affirmed the check and balance of

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.904
of a judicial judicial

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.241
where they can overrule legislative

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.977
laws that are unconstitutional.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.113
That's a foundational in our country.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.348
Those checks and balances are important

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.783
but in this election,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.952
we do need serious candidates,

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.321
people of courage and integrity.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.689
And that's why

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.623
I think Iowa

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.190
and New Hampshire

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.192
is going to do a good job

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.827
of sorting through that.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:08.161
All right.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.262
We'll see

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.197
how this unfolds for you as well.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.499
Governor Asa Hutchinson, thank

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:13.266
you very much.

